  "notes": "# DevClash 0.1.0-beta.3\n\nSign in to the desktop app using the same Google, Apple or email options as the DevClash website, with faster history uploads and clearer sync progress.\n\n- Choose **Sign In With Browser**, complete sign-in on the DevClash website, and enter the connection code shown in your app.\n- The desktop connects automatically after approval. An existing browser session can be used without another email code.\n- Connection requests expire after ten minutes. Cancel or retry from the desktop if needed.\n- Cloud uploads and public rankings remain separate opt-ins. Existing display preferences are preserved.\n- Large history uploads do less disk work, with safe checkpoint recovery if the app closes or the connection fails.\n- The dashboard and account settings show matching sync status and the remaining record count. Progress updates after each acknowledged background batch, and recovered errors clear as uploads resume.\n- Last Completed Sync identifies when the queue finished uploading, including the initial history upload.\n\nThis remains a beta. Windows may display a SmartScreen reputation warning despite valid publisher signing. Linux validation covers XFCE/X11; Wayland and physical Intel Mac validation remain limited as recorded for beta.2.\n\nRelease scope: full-release\nSource build: 0f8277444ce6c585148f9664ecb81517e90fd390\nSigned release workflow: 37770540719\n",
